course: dictionary
lesson: 9662
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Substance can mean a kind of material, the main point of something, or something real rather than just talk. Read the words around it, then ask: what would fit here?
explain: «Mars looks red because its dust contains iron oxide, the same kind of substance as rust.» Here substance means a kind of material. The clue is "the same kind of", and rust is a material, so iron oxide is too.
explain: «An indicator is a substance whose colour shows whether something is acidic or alkaline.» Here substance means a material with particular qualities. Test it: put "material" in place of "substance", and the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Substance means a material or kind of matter, such as water, salt or iron.
fact: «An indicator is a substance whose colour shows whether something is acidic or alkaline.»
fact: Solids, liquids and gases are all substances.
fact: A pure substance has only one kind of material; a mixture has two or more.
fact: Never touch, smell closely or taste harmful substances; look for warning symbols and tell an adult.
exercise: «Mars looks red because its dust contains iron oxide, the same kind of substance as rust.» In this sentence, what does substance mean? | *A kind of material | The main point of a story | A sticky sweet | Something that is only talk
exercise: A pure substance has only one kind of material. Which one is pure? | Sandy sea water | Vegetable soup | *Pure water | Muddy puddle water
exercise: Ella reads, «There was no substance to the rumour.» What does substance mean here? | A sticky mess | A kind of drink | *Something real, not just talk | A heavy, solid lump
test: In «an indicator is a substance whose colour shows whether something is acidic or alkaline», what is a substance? | *A material with particular qualities | A lesson in school | A loud sound | A person who tests things
test: The substance of a story means: | *Its main point or real meaning | Its cover and title | The number of pages | The loudest sound in it
exam: What should you do if you find an unknown harmful substance? | *Do not touch or taste it, and tell an adult | Smell it closely to find out | Taste a little to check what it is | Mix it with water to make it safe
